<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Locris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Locris was a region of ancient central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, divided into Eastern Locris on the Euboean Gulf and Western, or Ozolian, Locris on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-corinth">Gulf of Corinth</a>, separated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocis">Phocis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dori">Doris</a>. Its people, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a>, founded colonies such as Locri in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> parts of it were held by the Frankish lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and their neighbours.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/locris.jpg" alt="Locris" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Miller / After Hugh William Williams · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountains_of_Locri_Ozolae,_looking_towards_Naupactus_engraving_by_William_Miller_after_H_W_Williams.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
